---
import BookingButton from "../../common/BookingButton.astro";

/*
 * Section 5 — what it costs.
 *
 * THE WORD "FROM" IS LOAD-BEARING ON BOTH FIGURES, and the copy file says so in as many
 * words. It sets a floor without promising a ceiling, which is the only reason a number
 * can be published here at all. "CAD $1,000" flat is a different and worse claim — it
 * promises a price before anyone has seen the scope. Do not tidy "from" out of either
 * sentence, and do not move the figures higher up the page.
 *
 * THIS PAGE IS ALLOWED A PRICE. The value-before-cost rule in CLAUDE.md is scoped to the
 * homepage; the workshop page has always been the exception that carries its own. What
 * is still never published is the payment schedule.
 *
 * THE CREDIT IS STATED, THE WINDOW IS NOT. "Half the workshop fee comes off the build
 * price" is approved copy and ships as written. The copy file's own [CONFIRM] list flags
 * that an open-ended credit is a liability that never closes — if a window is decided, it
 * belongs in the proposal rather than on this page, and this section should not grow a
 * caveat. Delete a line rather than caveat it; that rule applies here too.
 *
 * THE SECOND SUB-BODY POINTS AT /accounting's PRICE, and the two must agree. Both say
 * implementation starts from CAD $4,000. If one changes, the other is wrong the same
 * day — there is no shared constant for it because it is a sentence, not a token.
 */
---

<section class="section section--warm cost" id="what-it-costs">
  <div class="container cost__inner">
    <div class="section__head cost__head">
      <h2 class="section__title cost__title">
        From CAD $1,000, half of it credited if you build.
      </h2>
      <p class="section__lede">
        The fee follows the scope &mdash; how much of the operation we&rsquo;re examining
        and how many workflows are involved. It&rsquo;s agreed before the day is booked
        and doesn&rsquo;t change afterwards. If you go ahead with an implementation, half
        the workshop fee comes off the build price.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="cost__notes">
      <p class="cost__note">
        A single area is one day. A business large enough to need several areas examined
        is a larger engagement, priced accordingly, and we&rsquo;ll say so before you
        commit rather than after.
      </p>
      <p class="cost__note">
        Implementation starts from CAD $4,000, depending on what the work involves &mdash;
        which is precisely what the workshop establishes.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="cost__cta">
      <BookingButton location="ws-cost" block>
        Book your free 20-minute call
      </BookingButton>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* THE CONTAINER IS THE STANDARD WIDTH. It was narrowed to 940px first, which read
   * calmly on its own and wrongly in sequence: every other section on the page starts at
   * the same left edge, and an inset one breaks the vertical line the eye follows down
   * the page. What answers the real problem — a left-aligned head leaving a third of a
   * wide band empty — is the two-column note row below, which runs the full width and
   * fills it. That is the same fix /accounting's section 2 landed on. */
  .cost__head {
    max-width: none;
  }

  .cost__title {
    max-width: 24ch;
  }

  /* Two notes, side by side and separated by a rule rather than boxed. They are
   * qualifications on the sentence above them, not two more things being offered —
   * cards would give them the weight of an offer. */
  .cost__notes {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    column-gap: 40px;
    margin-top: 40px;
    padding-top: 28px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--ark-hairline);
  }

  .cost__note {
    font-size: var(--ark-body);
    line-height: var(--ark-lh-body);
    color: var(--ark-body-ink);
  }

  .cost__note + .cost__note {
    padding-left: 40px;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--ark-hairline);
  }

  .cost__cta {
    margin-top: 40px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .cost__notes {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      row-gap: 18px;
      margin-top: 28px;
      padding-top: 22px;
    }

    /* Stacked, a left border reads as a quote mark on the second note rather than as a
     * divider between two columns. */
    .cost__note + .cost__note {
      padding-left: 0;
      padding-top: 18px;
      border-left: 0;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--ark-hairline);
    }

    .cost__note {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }

    .cost__cta {
      margin-top: 30px;
    }
  }
</style>
